risks:
SEAM CONTINUITY ACROSS SEVEN INDEPENDENTLY BUILT SCENES. The risks are:
- projection maths and camera velocity at 224/225 and 374/375;
- sphere state at 524/525;
- the dot at (1114,540);
- the full-stop position and hairline extents, which depend on Instrument Serif metrics.

Mitigation:
(a) A single film.ts owned by the director, imported by every engineer: PALETTE, easings, FOCAL, project(), drawFloor(), camZ_s2/camZ_s3, camS1/worldToScreen, S5_DOT and TITLE_LAYOUT(). Also sphere.ts, with a pure sphereState(globalFrame) shared by s4 and s5.
(b) TITLE_LAYOUT is computed with measureText only after loadFont resolves (delayRender/continueRender), never hard-coded. Approximate values from the actual font files: 'First ' = 337px, 'Light' = 370px, W about 739, P about (1318,540).
(c) Each engineer renders their first and last local frames as stills, and the director diffs the pairs 119/120, 224/225, 374/375, 524/525, 599/600 and 704/705 at 50% onion-skin. Tolerance: 1px in position and zero colour drift on any vermilion element.
(d) Technology and geometry changes happen only under cover: on a hard hit (375 flare plus CA plus impact, 600 ignition) or on a near-black frame (119, 704).

PROCEDURAL ARTEFACTS THAT READ AS 'BROKEN'. The risks are:
- wagon-wheel strobing of transverse floor lines at up to 142 px/f against their 120-unit spacing;
- moiré and shimmer of thin lines near the horizon;
- segments exploding when a vertex passes behind the camera;
- brackets popping at the lens;
- additive particles blowing out to white when the sphere collapses;
- soft text from CSS-scaled bitmaps;
- fallback fonts.

Mitigation:
(a) Transverse lines fade out over 296-322, before speed passes about 40 px/f. Velocity-length speed dashes replace them; these are inherently motion-blurred and cannot strobe.
(b) Fog per 600-unit segment (smoothstep 2200 to 7500) kills distant lines before they alias. Lines are at least 1.25px, positions rounded to 0.5px, lineCap 'butt'.
(c) Near-plane clipping (depth >= 60) runs before projection. No CSS 3D anywhere.
(d) Brackets fade with smoothstep(160, 400, depth) and are culled below 160; the s3 manual blur covers the fastest passes.
(e) In s5, particle alpha is multiplied by smoothstep(0, 0.3, rf) during the collapse, so the vermilion core glow carries the colour instead of a white blob.
(f) The s1 zoom is SVG text under a viewBox camera, so glyphs re-rasterise at 6x. will-change is overridden to auto on every scaling text layer. The shockwave and rays are soft gradients rather than sub-2px strokes, and the per-frame-seeded heat haze was cut.
(g) Every text scene gates on document.fonts.load via delayRender. Typing and blinks are the only linear motion, and they are deliberate.
